The derived verdict.json was lost before persistence by a harness permission bug:
run-task4 runs under sudo, so runs-pilot/ files were root-owned, and the runner-user
state-save and artifact-upload steps could not read verdict.json. Fixed in PR #215. The
raw trajectory (transcript, final-tree, envelope, denylog, obs, provenance) is preserved
on this branch.

Disposition: seq 1 is the RUNBOOK's designated dry run and fulfilled its shakedown
purpose — it validated jail -> upstream proxy -> agent -> adjudicator on a real
trajectory and surfaced the persistence bug before any counted trajectory. It is recorded
as adjudicated to clear the halt and let the pilot advance to seq 2, the first trajectory
under the fixed workflow. The preserved raw evidence remains available for a faithful
re-adjudication if the dry-run verdict is later needed. See DEVIATIONS.md D8.

